GC_LobbyGameMode : "{A79C4E0A43DEB821}Prefabs/MP/Modes/GC_LobbyGameMode.et" {
 ID "B0D9B20A7E559427"
 components {
  GC_LobbyManager "{6A137A39106A4973}" {
   m_aMissionEvents + {
    GC_Event "{8C0F1921C80B614E}" {
     m_sName "Opfor Victory by Time Limit (event 4, 3900s)"
     m_Advanced GC_EventOptions "{7476F5730E93B8CC}" {
      m_fDelay 3900
     }
     m_aActions {
      GC_MessageAction "{EC2809CE896CA968}" {
       m_sTitle "Time Limit Reached"
       m_sMessage "Insurgents WIN!"
      }
     }
    }
   }
   m_aBriefings {
    GC_Briefing "{BAFBD37A4631C249}" {
     m_iOrder 0
     m_sTitle "Overview"
     m_sContent "Late 2003, early operations in the Pech River Valley, Kunar Province, Afghanistan. US Army conducts sweeps through the valley, seeking weapons caches and establishing a presence to disrupt insurgent networks."\
     ""\
     "Special thanks to Haesten for his service and for assisting me to make the unit loadouts in this mission as accurate as possible, within reason, based on his own experiences/deployments."\
     ""\
     "Mission created by Gabe"
     m_eAudience 1
    }
    GC_Briefing "{B2E3A036FB19F371}" {
     m_iOrder 1
     m_sTitle "CIVILIAN BRIEFING"
     m_sContent "You spawn in pairs, your corresponding group number is marked on the map so you know where you spawn. Only you and your fellow civilians see this. "\
     ""\
     "Mission (required): roleplay as delivery drivers, drug dealers, or whatever your imagination can come up with. Conduct deliveries at each of the zones. Your job is to create a dynamic civilian experience. You are not a combatant, do not kill or harm either team. IF US FORCES TELL YOU TO MOVE AWAY FROM THEM, AND YOU DON'T, DON'T WHINE IF YOU END UP GETTING KILLED."\
     ""\
     "You may NOT pick up weapons or grenades of any kind. You MAY, however, choose to lean your allegiances to one side over the other, and provide intel to that side should you have any information to give. "\
     ""\
     "HMMWVs are locked to CIVs so don't bother trying to enter the FOB to take them if the US leaves them beheind."\
     ""\
     "Mission maker's intent is that you choose to do this based on your experience in the game, rather than having any kind of meta-game bias against the players on one team versus the other. If you feel that the insurgents are treating you poorly, turn on them and give up their locations to the Americans. If the Americans treat you poorly, maybe you end up being given a radio by the insurgents and give the insurgents real time strategic information."\
     ""\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "CIV"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{598FD896D3D113AC}" {
     m_iOrder 2
     m_sTitle "Situation Enemy"
     m_sContent "Up to 3 cells, including their HQ section, of Afghan insurgents equipped with AKs and bolt-action rifles. Expect use of old Soviet disposable RPGs. Previous engagements have included the use of a PKM as well."\
     ""\
     "Our marked green zone is no longer accessible to the enemy thanks to heightened security."\
     ""\
     "ENEMY MLCOA: Guerrilla tactics, shoot-and-scoot, delay our movement and blend in with civilian population, rinse and repeat. Use of explosives expected."\
     ""\
     "ENEMY MDCOA: Utilize their limited assets aggressively in an attempt to cause mass casualties to friendly forces. Use of VBIED (vehicle-borne improvised explosive device). Aggressive use of other IEDs and RPGs to inflict mass amounts of damage to friendly forces in a short amount of time."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{B22492FD52CD5A75}" {
     m_iOrder 3
     m_sTitle "Situation Enemy"
     m_sContent "Location marked by blue marker on the map, at their base. Enemy is a US Army Rifle Platoon armed with superior equipment from body armor to HMG-mounted Hummers, and limited optics. They frequently go on patrols and have been pushing farther and farther east in recent days."\
     ""\
     "West of Richahlam is their \"green zone\" and to cross into that is certain death."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_INSURGENT"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{0FC38DC523E11597}" {
     m_iOrder 4
     m_sTitle "Situation Friendly"
     m_sContent "Location marked on map at FOB Thunderbolt. US Army Rifle Platoon, up to 3x rifle squads and a weapons squad consisting of 2x M240B machine gun teams and 1x anti-tank team (Carl Gustaf), plus HQ which consists of a platoon leader, a platoon sergeant, and a medic."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{1DF11500D35FB0E4}" {
     m_iOrder 5
     m_sTitle "Situation Friendly"
     m_sContent "Location marked by red marker on map. We are located east of Richahlam. We have AKs, bolt-action rifles, a couple disposable RPGs, some weapons caches to our east to fall back on, and most importantly, Allah. "\
     ""\
     "We have a sapper and his explosive-rigged vehicle (parked across from the other vehicles so you know which one is rigged with explosives)."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_INSURGENT"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{AEDB3CA6FFA36F20}" {
     m_iOrder 6
     m_sTitle "Mission"
     m_sContent "The US Army must successfully sweep and clear at least 3 of the 4 objective areas of insurgents within 60 minutes (excluding 5 minute setup timer). "\
     ""\
     "Mission failure if:"\
     "     - US takes 65% casualties"\
     "     - CIV takes 80% casualties"\
     ""\
     "Objective Options:"\
     "     - Richahlam"\
     "     - Gas Station"\
     "     - Khandar Proper"\
     "     - Khandar Farm"\
     ""\
     "AN OBJECTIVE TAKEN NOTIFICATION WILL APPEAR IF BLUFOR MAKES UP 90% OF THE POPULATION IN THE MARKED AREA FOR ANY AMOUNT OF TIME. THIS DOES NOT TAKE CIVILIANS INTO ACCOUNT WHATSOEVER (i.e. Blufor has 9 soldiers in an objective area, Opfor has 2 but then 1 dies, Blufor takes the objective despite there being 1 Opfor still present as 9/10 = 0.90 = 90% of present non-civilian players in the area.)"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{A4673F44126C5308}" {
     m_iOrder 7
     m_sTitle "Mission"
     m_sContent "Conduct guerrilla warfare operations against the infidels as they push east today to patrol our land and villages. Delay them from conducting their patrols. If we can keep them from successfully patrolling 3 of the possible 4 marked areas on our maps over the next hour, then that is a victory."\
     ""\
     "Alternatively, kill 65% of them and send them back to their base in shambles."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_INSURGENT"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CEF4808ECDA64B04}" {
     m_iOrder 8
     m_sTitle "Execution"
     m_sContent "Decide which 3 objectives you want to patrol to and sweep, then determine a route, either relying on the roads or the hillsides (or both) to enable mutual support amongst your squads."\
     ""\
     "There is cover along the ASR (rock walls) should you choose to use it as a main axis with the HMMWVs supporting from the road. Alternatively, the dirt road headed through the villages is also traversable."\
     ""\
     "You can optionally use up to 2x M2 HMMWVs (see Service and Support)"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{7D756C2680A3BF20}" {
     m_iOrder 9
     m_sTitle "Execution"
     m_sContent "The infidels have strict rules and will not shoot us if we look like the civilians. Occupy objective areas or surrounding areas in order to engage and delay the enemy US forces."\
     ""\
     "It is recommended that we try to carry as much of our inventory as possible in our shirts and pants to avoid using tactical vests where able in case we need to drop our gear/weapons and fall back. "\
     ""\
     "We can simply pretend to be part of the civilian population, fall back to one of our caches (marked on the map), and re-engage them."\
     ""\
     "Cache location number 3 has a couple extra disposable RPGs, it is suggested that we use the ones we have first before grabbing those since, as mentioned above, we may have to drop our weapons and gear to fall back without being shot at and killed. It would be a shame to lose all our RPGs early on in this fight!"\
     ""\
     ""\
     ""\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_INSURGENT"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{AC1145691A179EEB}" {
     m_iOrder 10
     m_sTitle "Command and Signals"
     m_sContent "Platoon HQ -- Bravo 1'6"\
     "Platoon Sgt. - Bravo 1'7"\
     "1st Squad ---- Bravo 1'1"\
     "2nd Squad --- Bravo 1'2"\
     "3rd Squad ---- Bravo 1'3"\
     "Weapons ----- Bravo 1'4"\
     ""\
     "Platoon Net - 48.00 MHz"\
     ""\
     "Squad Nets: NONE, team leaders have the same PRC-68 radio as squad leader, with a range of 500 meters."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{815CED524184EE28}" {
     m_iOrder 11
     m_sTitle "Command and Signals"
     m_sContent "Pech Cell HQ - Command"\
     "Pech Cell 1 --- 1"\
     "Pech Cell 2 --- 2"\
     ""\
     "Intercell communication - 42.00 MHz"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_INSURGENT"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{86965D2BCD68794F}" {
     m_iOrder 12
     m_sTitle "Service and Support"
     m_sContent "Up to 3x U.S. Army squads of up to 9 men each. LAWs, M249s, M4s equipped with M203s and close-range optics, team leads have ACOGs instead of binoculars for M249 spotting. Each LAT rifleman has 1x M249 box and 1x 7.62 box for the M240B."\
     ""\
     "Up to 1x weapons squad of up to 7 men, 2x M240B machine gun teams consisting of the gunner and an MG assistant with an ACOG scoped M4 for spotting. 1000 rounds per gun including crossloaded rounds on the weapons squad leader. Each rifle squad also has 200 more 7.62 rounds split between the two LAT rifleman (1 box each). 1x Carl Gustaf team with 4x HEAT rounds between the two of them."\
     ""\
     "2x M2 HMMWV optionally available for use loaded with some extra medical equipment, magazines, M249 boxes, and 40mm grenade launcher ammunition."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{123FF4003B17C85C}" {
     m_iOrder 13
     m_sTitle "Ammo and Cache Information"
     m_sContent "Up to 2x cells plus an HQ section of up to 4-6 men each. Soviet-era small arms. RPGs, other AK variants, bolt-action rifles, and a medic. We have 1x PKM gun and 1x VBIED."\
     ""\
     "AMMO BOX AT SPAWN WITH 5x radios. Use them however you'd like."\
     ""\
     "Our caches have limited extra 7.62 ammo for the bolt-action and AKs which use it, however, if you drop your weapon and fallback, you will only be able to grab an AK-74 and 5.45 magazines from the caches. There are limited amounts of grenades at the caches as well, use them wisely. Cache location number 3 also has 2 extra disposable RPGs."\
     ""\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_INSURGENT"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{C6CC82263BF6C3B2}" {
     m_iOrder 14
     m_sTitle "Notes & End Conditions (MUST READ)"
     m_sContent "Civilians may NOT wander off into the mountains to have a party of their own separate from the rest of the playerbase. They are expected to exist nearby the other players, roleplaying as civilians making deliveries and/or going about their daily lives. Should they align more with one side than the other, they may provide intel or receive radios to provide intel. They may not become combatants of any kind, however."\
     ""\
     "Insurgents can drop their gear and retreat further back into the AO without being killed. US MUST NOT metagame and kill an unarmed insurgent just because they know which person it is and they know said person is on the enemy team. "\
     ""\
     "GMs should revive insurgents who get executed for no good reason. Attempting to retreat with a weapon in your hand or while wearing a tactical vest IS good reason to be killed, for example, but an insurgent who drops their gun and tactical vest should be assumed to be a civilian. "\
     ""\
     "Civilians wear rucksacks sometimes - a ruck is not an indication of being a combatant."\
     ""\
     "The US Army must successfully sweep and clear at least 3 of the 4 objective areas of insurgents within 60 minutes (excluding 5 minute setup timer). "\
     ""\
     "Objective is taken by Blufor making up 90% of the population (not including civilians)"\
     ""\
     "US Army loses if:"\
     "     - They take 65% casualties"\
     "     - They kill 80% of the player civilians"\
     "     - They fail to complete the objective in time"\
     ""\
     "Insurgents lose if:"\
     "     - They take 90% casualties"\
     "     - US Army completes their objective in time"
     m_eAudience 2
    }
   }
  }
 }
}
